I don't know. That would have had its own

00:13:36.820 --> 00:13:40.100
share of problems.
Speaker 3: Yeah. And part of the book is really

00:13:40.100 --> 00:13:43.840
not saying direct is the solution. As much
as direct is the cornerstone. And a cornerstone

00:13:43.840 --> 00:13:48.530
really is a very, very small piece of a much
larger, larger edifice. So the point is saying

00:13:48.530 --> 00:13:53.190
we've gotten to this hyper intermediated world
where generally speaking, the instinct was

00:13:53.190 --> 00:13:57.581
always to add additional layers of middlemen.
But as you nicely point out earlier, there's

00:13:57.581 --> 00:14:02.040
already a countermovement underway. There's
already a number of people saying to be able

00:14:02.040 --> 00:14:05.910
to really get what I want, to have my values
match my actions. I need to opt out of the

00:14:05.910 --> 00:14:13.600
system entirely. And so by documenting both
the growth of this hyper intermediated world

00:14:13.600 --> 00:14:18.830
and this revolution, well, then we can figure
out how to navigate this territory in between.

00:14:18.830 --> 00:14:23.780
And the toilet paper is a great example of
it. So as you're pointing out, the nature

00:14:23.780 --> 00:14:27.450
of the supply chains had incredible rigidities,
which just meant like they were used to doing

00:14:27.450 --> 00:14:32.080
one thing and they couldn't easily change.
Right. And oftentimes what we're seeing with

00:14:32.080 --> 00:14:37.431
those rigidities, the complexity really accentuates
them. And it's not about going direct, but

00:14:37.431 --> 00:14:44.060
having fewer middlemen and shorter chains
can oftentimes enhance resilience and enhance

00:14:44.060 --> 00:14:50.250
flexibility. So trying to figure out where
did we add layers over time without anybody

00:14:50.250 --> 00:14:55.200
really understanding, well, what are the needs
of the world where things might go wrong and

00:14:55.200 --> 00:14:58.790
where that might create problems? Or going
back to our earlier conversation, where there

00:14:58.790 --> 00:15:02.980
might be a lack of accountability, because
now there's just no way for us to actually

00:15:02.980 --> 00:15:08.029
see through all of the different layers involved.
